1
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:04,840
It's the end of the

2
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:05,790
year.

3
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:06,950
The rainy season should be

4
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:07,850
here.

5
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:09,270
So why does Singapore still

6
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:10,743
feel like an oven?

7
00:00:10,743 --> 00:00:12,688
My fur is melting!

8
00:00:12,688 --> 00:00:13,878
My water bowl went down

9
00:00:13,878 --> 00:00:14,947
again.

10
00:00:14,947 --> 00:00:15,537
I feel great,

11
00:00:15,537 --> 00:00:16,557
actually.

12
00:00:16,557 --> 00:00:18,266
Lizards love the heat!

13
00:00:18,266 --> 00:00:19,476
Not us!

14
00:00:19,476 --> 00:00:20,766
Drink lots of water and

15
00:00:20,766 --> 00:00:22,506
stay in the shade.

16
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:24,608
The answer starts thousands of

17
00:00:24,608 --> 00:00:25,918
kilometres away,

18
00:00:25,918 --> 00:00:27,748
over the Pacific Ocean.

19
00:00:27,748 --> 00:00:28,868
Let's shrink down and go

20
00:00:28,868 --> 00:00:29,958
there.

21
00:00:30,202 --> 00:00:31,462
Are you ready?

22
00:00:31,462 --> 00:00:32,502
Three!

23
00:00:32,502 --> 00:00:33,492
Two!

24
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:34,492
One!

25
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:35,652
Go!

26
00:00:40,093 --> 00:00:40,943
You are a gust of

27
00:00:40,943 --> 00:00:42,133
wind.

28
00:00:42,313 --> 00:00:43,523
You blow over the Pacific

29
00:00:43,523 --> 00:00:45,413
Ocean from east to west,

30
00:00:45,413 --> 00:00:47,073
day after day.

31
00:00:47,223 --> 00:00:48,383
People call you the trade

32
00:00:48,383 --> 00:00:49,653
wind.

33
00:00:49,899 --> 00:00:50,599
Below you,

34
00:00:50,599 --> 00:00:52,279
the sea is warm.

35
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:53,669
You push the warm top

36
00:00:53,669 --> 00:00:54,879
layer of water along with

37
00:00:54,879 --> 00:00:55,459
you,

38
00:00:55,459 --> 00:00:56,159
west,

39
00:00:56,159 --> 00:00:57,929
towards Singapore.

40
00:00:58,165 --> 00:00:59,495
The warm water gains heat

41
00:00:59,495 --> 00:01:00,925
from the Sun.

42
00:01:01,095 --> 00:01:02,515
Some of it evaporates into

43
00:01:02,515 --> 00:01:04,435
water vapour and rises with

44
00:01:04,435 --> 00:01:05,395
you.

45
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:06,185
High up,

46
00:01:06,185 --> 00:01:08,345
the water vapour loses heat,

47
00:01:08,345 --> 00:01:10,625
condenses into tiny water droplets

48
00:01:10,625 --> 00:01:12,555
and forms clouds.

49
00:01:12,807 --> 00:01:13,977
Over Singapore,

50
00:01:13,977 --> 00:01:16,026
the clouds rain down.

51
00:01:16,177 --> 00:01:18,317
That is a normal year.

52
00:01:19,159 --> 00:01:20,079
But this year,

53
00:01:20,079 --> 00:01:22,259
you grow weaker and weaker.

54
00:01:22,469 --> 00:01:24,009
The warm water slides back

55
00:01:24,009 --> 00:01:24,789
east,

56
00:01:24,789 --> 00:01:26,719
away from Singapore.

57
00:01:26,859 --> 00:01:27,529
The warm,

58
00:01:27,529 --> 00:01:28,949
wet air that rises from

59
00:01:28,949 --> 00:01:29,489
it,

60
00:01:29,489 --> 00:01:31,189
and builds the rain clouds,

61
00:01:31,189 --> 00:01:32,779
moves east too.

62
00:01:32,779 --> 00:01:33,419
Wait for us,

63
00:01:33,419 --> 00:01:34,909
clouds!

64
00:01:35,145 --> 00:01:36,975
In strong El Niño years,

65
00:01:36,975 --> 00:01:38,305
the warm water spreads over

66
00:01:38,305 --> 00:01:39,935
coral reefs.

67
00:01:40,105 --> 00:01:41,665
A reef is the habitat

68
00:01:41,665 --> 00:01:43,590
of many sea animals.

69
00:01:43,590 --> 00:01:44,870
Too much heat turns the

70
00:01:44,870 --> 00:01:46,470
corals white.

71
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:49,040
This is called coral bleaching.

72
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:50,480
If it lasts too long,

73
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,170
the corals die.

74
00:01:52,812 --> 00:01:54,352
Near South America,

75
00:01:54,352 --> 00:01:55,842
the small fish become hard

76
00:01:55,842 --> 00:01:57,222
to find.

77
00:01:57,392 --> 00:01:59,072
Sea lions and seabirds go

78
00:01:59,072 --> 00:01:59,952
hungry,

79
00:01:59,952 --> 00:02:01,112
and many of their babies

80
00:02:01,112 --> 00:02:02,069
die.

81
00:02:02,069 --> 00:02:03,289
Oh no.

82
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:05,309
The poor little pups.

83
00:02:05,852 --> 00:02:07,242
Back near Singapore,

84
00:02:07,242 --> 00:02:08,252
ponds dry up,

85
00:02:08,252 --> 00:02:09,112
and the fish in them

86
00:02:09,112 --> 00:02:10,322
die.

87
00:02:10,462 --> 00:02:12,012
Dry peat forests burn,

88
00:02:12,012 --> 00:02:14,570
and orangutans lose their home.

89
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:16,166
Somebody help them!

90
00:02:16,166 --> 00:02:18,086
Rescue teams do.

91
00:02:18,256 --> 00:02:20,046
They carry orangutans to safer

92
00:02:20,046 --> 00:02:21,265
forests.

93
00:02:21,265 --> 00:02:22,685
When a habitat changes too

94
00:02:22,685 --> 00:02:23,465
much,

95
00:02:23,465 --> 00:02:25,225
living things must adapt,

96
00:02:25,225 --> 00:02:26,555
move to other places,

97
00:02:26,555 --> 00:02:27,965
or die.

98
00:02:28,806 --> 00:02:31,116
You look down at Singapore.

99
00:02:31,296 --> 00:02:32,816
Blue sky.

100
00:02:33,006 --> 00:02:35,296
Hardly any rain clouds.

101
00:02:35,466 --> 00:02:36,406
What you just lived through

102
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:38,896
has a name: El Niño.

103
00:02:39,933 --> 00:02:41,413
On the twelfth of November,

104
00:02:41,413 --> 00:02:42,773
scientists at NOAA in the

105
00:02:42,773 --> 00:02:44,693
USA said this El Niño

106
00:02:44,693 --> 00:02:46,663
is strong to very strong.

107
00:02:46,663 --> 00:02:47,413
Back in May,

108
00:02:47,413 --> 00:02:49,323
Singapore's weather scientists had already

109
00:02:49,323 --> 00:02:51,253
warned us: a warmer,

110
00:02:51,253 --> 00:02:53,543
drier June to October.

111
00:02:53,792 --> 00:02:55,142
The middle of the Pacific

112
00:02:55,142 --> 00:02:57,092
is more than 2 degrees Celsius

113
00:02:57,092 --> 00:02:58,662
warmer than usual.

114
00:02:58,662 --> 00:02:59,992
When it gets that warm,

115
00:02:59,992 --> 00:03:01,442
scientists call it a Super

116
00:03:01,442 --> 00:03:02,646
El Niño.

117
00:03:02,646 --> 00:03:04,473
Only 2 degrees?

118
00:03:04,473 --> 00:03:05,983
Across a whole ocean,

119
00:03:05,983 --> 00:03:07,163
that is a huge amount

120
00:03:07,163 --> 00:03:08,343
of heat.

121
00:03:09,191 --> 00:03:11,021
Let's name what you saw.

122
00:03:11,021 --> 00:03:13,001
Water gains heat and evaporates

123
00:03:13,001 --> 00:03:14,751
to form water vapour.

124
00:03:14,751 --> 00:03:16,711
When water vapour loses heat,

125
00:03:16,711 --> 00:03:19,101
it changes into water droplets.

126
00:03:19,101 --> 00:03:21,711
This process is called condensation,

127
00:03:21,711 --> 00:03:22,731
where a change in state

128
00:03:22,731 --> 00:03:25,181
from gas to liquid occurs.

129
00:03:25,181 --> 00:03:27,211
The droplets fall as rain.

130
00:03:27,211 --> 00:03:28,851
The continuous movement of water

131
00:03:28,851 --> 00:03:29,681
from the Earth to the

132
00:03:29,681 --> 00:03:31,221
sky and back to the

133
00:03:31,221 --> 00:03:32,561
Earth again is called the

134
00:03:32,561 --> 00:03:33,911
water cycle.

135
00:03:33,911 --> 00:03:35,221
El Niño does not stop

136
00:03:35,221 --> 00:03:36,621
the water cycle.

137
00:03:36,621 --> 00:03:37,541
It moves where the rain

138
00:03:37,541 --> 00:03:38,831
falls.

139
00:03:39,877 --> 00:03:40,947
With less rain,

140
00:03:40,947 --> 00:03:42,297
forests and peatland in our

141
00:03:42,297 --> 00:03:43,887
region dried out.

142
00:03:43,887 --> 00:03:45,857
Dry land burns easily,

143
00:03:45,857 --> 00:03:47,127
so the fires that started

144
00:03:47,127 --> 00:03:49,477
burned longer and spread further.

145
00:03:49,477 --> 00:03:50,867
On the ninth of October,

146
00:03:50,867 --> 00:03:52,367
Singapore's haze reading,

147
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:53,627
the PSI,

148
00:03:53,627 --> 00:03:55,927
reached 192.

149
00:03:55,927 --> 00:03:57,537
That is unhealthy.

150
00:03:57,537 --> 00:03:59,117
Remember the smoke particle from

151
00:03:59,117 --> 00:04:00,496
Episode 1?

152
00:04:00,496 --> 00:04:02,556
Even I stayed indoors.

153
00:04:03,201 --> 00:04:04,981
El Niño moves rain around

154
00:04:04,981 --> 00:04:06,041
the world.

155
00:04:06,041 --> 00:04:06,821
In India,

156
00:04:06,821 --> 00:04:08,431
this year's monsoon brought about

157
00:04:08,431 --> 00:04:10,511
one-eighth less rain than normal,

158
00:04:10,511 --> 00:04:11,801
the weakest in over ten

159
00:04:11,801 --> 00:04:12,801
years.

160
00:04:12,801 --> 00:04:14,131
The south and the northeast

161
00:04:14,131 --> 00:04:15,551
were driest.

162
00:04:15,802 --> 00:04:16,862
In the USA,

163
00:04:16,862 --> 00:04:17,832
it works the other way

164
00:04:17,832 --> 00:04:19,452
for some places.

165
00:04:19,452 --> 00:04:20,222
This winter,

166
00:04:20,222 --> 00:04:22,282
scientists expect wetter weather than

167
00:04:22,282 --> 00:04:24,062
usual across the south,

168
00:04:24,062 --> 00:04:26,062
like California and Florida,

169
00:04:26,062 --> 00:04:27,112
and a warmer winter up

170
00:04:27,112 --> 00:04:28,131
north.

171
00:04:28,131 --> 00:04:30,061
So one tired wind changes

172
00:04:30,061 --> 00:04:32,118
the weather in three countries?

173
00:04:32,118 --> 00:04:33,218
Yes.

174
00:04:33,218 --> 00:04:34,728
That is why scientists all

175
00:04:34,728 --> 00:04:36,528
over the world watch it.

176
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:38,650
Be a weather detective.

177
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:39,610
Put two cups with the

178
00:04:39,610 --> 00:04:41,790
same amount of water outside:

179
00:04:41,790 --> 00:04:42,920
one in the sun,

180
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,430
one in the shade.

181
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:46,150
Mark the water level.

182
00:04:46,150 --> 00:04:47,940
Check after three days.

183
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:49,260
Which cup lost more water,

184
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:50,330
and why?

185
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:51,680
Hint: which one gained more

186
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:52,850
heat?

187
00:04:53,704 --> 00:04:54,694
Then tell a friend in

188
00:04:54,694 --> 00:04:56,674
India or the USA what

189
00:04:56,674 --> 00:04:57,864
El Niño is doing to

190
00:04:57,864 --> 00:04:59,092
their weather!

191
00:04:59,092 --> 00:05:00,002
See you next time on

192
00:05:00,002 --> 00:05:00,742
TheOneApp,

193
00:05:00,742 --> 00:05:02,032
Explored.

194
00:05:02,245 --> 00:05:04,404
Now you know!
